  "final_message": "Partial refunds are in. `refund_invoice`, `BillingEngine.refund` and `POST /invoices/{id}/refund` now take an optional `amount` in minor units. The suite passes: 37 tests, the 24 existing plus 13 new in `tests/test_refunds.py`.\n\n**What changed**\n- **`billing/refunds.py`**: `refund_invoice` takes `amount=None`. With an amount, it refunds that much through the gateway, oldest successful payment first. A payment becomes `partially_refunded`, or `refunded` once fully repaid. Each call creates one `refunded=True` credit note for the refunded amount.\n- **Without an amount**, it refunds all remaining money and returns applied credit once. After partial refunds it refunds only the remainder.\n- **Errors**: an amount that is `<= 0`, not an integer, or above the remaining refundable money raises `ValidationError`. If nothing is left to refund, it raises `InvalidStateError`.\n- **`billing/engine.py`** and **`billing/api.py`**: plumb `amount` through. The API uses a new `_optional_int` helper and returns 400 for a non-integer amount.\n- **`answer.json`**: written at the repo root. Git ignores it through `.gitignore`, so it does not show in `git status`.\n\n**Decisions to review**\n- **Credit returned by a full refund is zeroed on the invoice.** I used the existing `restore_credit` helper, which sets `credit_applied` to 0. Without that, a second full refund could return the same credit again. Previously the field stayed populated after a refund. Invoice rendering and JSON will now show no credit line after a full refund.\n- **Refunds stay blocked after any non-refunded credit note**, as they were before. Only refunded notes stop blocking, so partial refunds can continue.\n- **Credit is never returned by a partial refund.** It comes back only on a full refund.\n\n**Not addressed**\n- If the gateway refuses a later payment in a multi-payment refund, the earlier gateway refunds have already gone through and are not rolled back. This was already true of the old full-refund loop.\n- `credit_invoice` still counts refunded notes against the invoice total, so it can be limited after a partial refund. I left it alone because it was outside the request.\n\nI did not commit anything.",
